content.text:
I created `index.html` with Tandem and it passed every check the job ran: 2 checks and 30 constraints, all on the first try with no repairs needed.

Those checks loaded the page in a browser and confirmed:
- it starts paused with 60 boids, and the button reads Play;
- Play/Pause, Step, Reset and the speed slider (0.5–3.0) work;
- clicking the canvas adds a boid, and the HUD count goes up right away;
- the background is #070b14 and the HUD has the blur effect.

I didn't open the file or watch the console myself, so "zero JavaScript errors" rests on the requirements I set for the job. No test asserted it on its own.

Everything is in that one file, with no external dependencies.

